    "and the bread it makes is slightly sour and keeps fresh for longer. Different places made different "
    "breads from what grew there: flat breads baked on hot stones, dark rye loaves in the cold north, white "
    "rolls in the cities once mills could grind fine flour cheaply. Today a small bakery and a large factory "
    "follow the same steps, only at different speeds. The factory mixes the dough in minutes with machines and "
